  × This computed property runs asynchronous code.
  
    2 │ import { computed } from "vue";
    3 │ 
  > 4 │ const nonNullCallee = computed(() => bar.then!(() => {}));
      │                                      ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
    5 │ const withTypeArguments = computed<number>(async () => 1);
    6 │ const typeAssertion = computed(() => (Promise as PromiseConstructor).resolve(1));
  
  i Vue uses the value that a computed property returns right away. Asynchronous code finishes later, so its result never becomes the value of the computed property.
  
  i Store the result in a ref() or in data from a watcher or a method, and read it from the computed property instead.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  

